    {
      "id": 45,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -680,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        640,
        1100
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 44,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX.2 [klein]: text-to-image, references, Hires. fix\n\n[FLUX.2 [klein]](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-9b-fp8) (Black Forest Labs, 9B, Qwen3 8B text\nencoder) is a fast step-distilled text-to-image and multi-reference editing model, set up here with every Generate\ntab feature that ComfyUI offers for it. Write full descriptive sentences and put literal text in quotes.\n\n**Settings (distilled, this workflow)**: 4 steps, CFG 1, euler, `Flux2Scheduler`, 1024×1024 (multiples of 16).\nThe negative conditioning is zeroed (**ConditioningZeroOut**): at CFG 1 there is no negative pass, so the Generate tab\nshows no negative prompt. Raising CFG burns the image.\n\n**Base** (`flux-2-klein-base-9b-fp8`, undistilled, for LoRA training or true CFG): pick it in the model list, set 20-30\nsteps and CFG about 4. For a negative prompt, replace **ConditioningZeroOut** with a **CLIP Text Encode** titled\n`ib:np`, fed by the clip output of the Image Bench Prompt and passed through Reference Latent nodes of its own if\nyou use references.\n\n**klein 4B** (Apache-2.0): `flux-2-klein-4b-fp8` with the `qwen_3_4b` text encoder in **Load CLIP**, same settings.\nLoRAs and ControlNets of FLUX.2 [dev] do not load on klein (a different transformer).\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:pp` | Image Bench Prompt | prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | SamplerCustomAdvanced | seed (RandomNoise), steps (Flux2Scheduler), sampling method, CFG scale (CFGGuider), size (Width / Height) |\n| `ib:smp:1` | Hires. fix sampler | Hires. fix: upscaler (Hires. fix upscaler), scale (Hires. fix scale), steps (Hires. fix scheduler), denoising (Hires. fix denoise) |\n| `ib:hr` | Hires. fix (If/Else Switch) | Hires. fix checkbox; switched on by the Upscale button |\n| `ib:ref:0-3` | Reference 1-4 (bypassed) | References panel |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**References** (up to 4; klein takes up to 10, add slots by copying a column and numbering its loader\n`ib:ref:4`, ...): add images in the References panel of the Generate tab (a tab next to LoRA), by \"Ps sends to:\nreference\" from Photoshop, or by dropping them there. An empty slot is bypassed together with its scale and encode\nnodes; its **Reference Latent** stays and passes the conditioning on unchanged. Refer to the references by order in\nthe prompt (*\"the woman from image 1 wearing the jacket from image 2\"*); for an edit, say what changes and what stays\n(*\"change the jacket to red leather, keep the face, pose and background\"*). Each is scaled to 1 MP first. The zeroed\nnegative keeps the references, so they also act in the negative pass of the base model.\n\n**Hires. fix** upscales the first pass to *Upscale by* (1.5×), encodes it again and samples the last *denoising*\npart of a schedule computed for the new size: 8 hires steps at 0.4 run 3 steps. It shares noise, guider (and so the\nCFG scale) and sampler with the first pass. The distilled model needs few steps; above about 0.5 it redraws details.\n\n**Upscaler**: **Hires. fix upscaler** (`Load Upscale Model`, the Upscaler list of the Generate tab)\nenlarges the first pass by its own factor, and **Resize to the hires size** brings it to the first pass size ×\n*Upscale by* (**Hires. fix scale** only computes that size). Put any ESRGAN-type model into\n`models/upscale_models` ([RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Real-ESRGAN_repackaged/resolve/main/RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors) here). The loader must name an installed model\neven while Hires. fix is off, since ComfyUI checks every node before running.\n\n**Hires. fix ib:hr** (`If/Else Switch`) is the Hires. fix checkbox of the Generate tab: on, it saves the\nHires. fix image; off, the first pass image, and the Hires. fix nodes do not run (its inputs are lazy). The\n**Upscale** button of the image lists switches it on, generates the image again with its seed and parameters, and\nswitches it back, so drafts made with Hires. fix off can be upscaled later (keep the size the same).\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt; the **Image Bench Prompt** node\napplies them. **Load LoRA** stays bypassed; LoRA exploration enables it for its runs and bypasses it again.\n\nBatch generation, model and LoRA exploration, varying parameters, PNG Info, projects and the Compare tab work\nas with every marked workflow. The ControlNet tab has no units here: ComfyUI has no ControlNet for klein; use a pose\nor depth map as a reference instead (*\"in the pose of image 2\"*).\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**: [flux-2-klein-9b-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-9b-fp8/resolve/main/flux-2-klein-9b-fp8.safetensors) (distilled), [flux-2-klein-base-9b-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-base-9b-fp8/resolve/main/flux-2-klein-base-9b-fp8.safetensors) (base)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein-9B/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors)\n**vae**: [full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-small-decoder/resolve/main/full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors)\n\nFLUX.2 [klein] 9B is released under the FLUX Non-Commercial License, klein 4B under Apache-2.0.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: FLUX.2 [dev] (Image Bench, all features)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
